gainst firearms now, after all. And then, shooting him might be hard... Urhan to act first, Predator's Unmatched Pursuit to move up close, then Hit and Run to vanish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can he defend against the Chunky Salsa rule in dealing with explosions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T04:44:48-07:00","id":680893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/129553-so-about-red-stick?p=680890#post680890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can he defend against the Chunky Salsa rule in dealing with explosions?</div> </div> </div> </div> What chunky salsa rule?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T04:51:10-07:00","id":680897,"title":"","content":"It's ignored by werewolves.<br /> <br /> P94, 'Only silver and supernatural powers (including Gifts, mage spells, and vampiric Disciplines) can cause aggravated damage to Uratha directly. Any source of harm that would cause aggravated damage to a human, including massive bodily devastation, only causes lethal damage to Uratha. '<br /> <br /> He might get by with just Primal Fear, which forces all lesser opponents to use the Down &amp; Dirty rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-28-2015, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T04:52:15-07:00","id":680899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/129553-so-about-red-stick?p=680893#post680893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What chunky salsa rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadowrun term. basically using a explosion in enclosed spaces where the force doesn't have enough force to break the container means that the force of the blast will rebound with slightly decreased but still lethal force, effectively meaning you're getting hit with a series of explosions over and over again until the force of the blast decreases to zero.<br /> <br /> The end result is.... well.. chucky salsa.<br /> <br /> WoD uses a different system, just wondering if it works somewhat similarly enough for it to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T06:28:13-07:00","id":680959,"title":"","content":"There's no chunky salsa rule in nWoD, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T06:56:04-07:00","id":680965,"title":"","content":"It would be a weird rule to have pitting one werewolf against a whole branch of a nation's military. You would need a very large enclosed space, which would then require a very large explosive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T07:28:01-07:00","id":680970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/129553-so-about-red-stick?p=680965#post680965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be a weird rule to have pitting one werewolf against a whole branch of a nation's military. You would need a very large enclosed space, which would then require a very large explosive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, honestly, I would expect them to just lace bombs with sliver and drop them. Worse come to worse, have a couple of drones fly up and start bombing again and again or a sniper team to fire sliver bullets with the element of surprise with flooding the area with people with sliver bullets.<br /> <br /> My mind went to Chunky Salsa mostly due to the Shadowrun game I just got done playing.<br /> <br /> Red Sticks has a lot of things in his toolkit, a few that can even sustain a short engagement with national forces coming after him. But after that, it's a done deal. A nation state will eventually find and kill him simply due to the firepower, Intel, and most importantly, persistence that they engage with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T07:31:01-07:00","id":680973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/129553-so-about-red-stick?p=680970#post680970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, honestly, I would expect them to just lace bombs with sliver and drop them. Worse come to worse, have a couple of drones fly up and start bombing again and again or a sniper team to fire sliver bullets with the element of surprise with flooding the area with people with sliver bullets.<br /> <br /> My mind went to Chunky Salsa mostly due to the Shadowrun game I just got done playing.<br /> <br /> Red Sticks has a lot of things in his toolkit, a few that can even sustain a short engagement with national forces coming after him. But after that, it's a done deal. A nation state will eventually find and kill him simply due to the firepower, Intel, and most importantly, persistence that they engage with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Most of those things get disregarded if he manages to get to the shadow, including lower Harmony from his cannibalistic wiles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T07:43:34-07:00","id":680976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/129553-so-about-red-stick?p=680973#post680973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of those things get disregarded if he manages to get to the shadow, including lower Harmony from his cannibalistic wiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tactics? yes. Strategy, no. For example: Israel's Mossid is still hunting down rumored Nazis to this day and with all the methods of evasion, OBL was still caught in the end.<br /> <br /> After all, it's not the like nation is going anywhere.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T09:16:40-07:00","id":681047,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but Bin Laden lasted 10 years without supernaturally assisted stealth, the ability to jump between worlds, the ability to turn onlookers into lunatics, a supernatural resistance to major damage as well as rapid regeneration. Not to mention literally superhuman Strength (9) and Stamina (8) among other attributes. And we're talking Hishu, here.<br /> <br /> He also had Ward Against Humans, which I probably translates to Boundary Ward in 2nd Ed - so Seal Team 6 would have been walking into an ambush. Not to mention that the book specifically says that he spends most his time in the Hisil and he is often guarded by packs of experienced Predator Kings.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think killing him would be a lot more difficult than you realize. Even with modern tactics and technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T09:59:10-07:00","id":681060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/129553-so-about-red-stick?p=681047#post681047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I think killing him would be a lot more difficult than you realize. Even with modern tactics and technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never said it wasn't. Just that nations are very, very persistent in whom they go after. They won't win today. They may not win for months on end.<br /> <br /> But once they have their sights on someone, they rarely give up. They're like zombies that way. You can fight (and easily defeat) them early on but the ruckus will always bring more and more resources upon your head. As powerful as he is, the other side has more people, more expertise, and to put quite frankly, more dice to roll over time.<br /> <br /> It's the case of a unstoppable force moving against an immovable object and given that type of treat with that kind of prolonged response, he's more likely to crack first.<br /> <br /> Still a moot point though. If you've gotten the attention of an entire nation's military (not just whatever their Tier 3 hunter org is), you've done goofed and made yourself an enemy of the Powers That Be will remove any trace of existence to maintain the Veil.<br /> <br /> Of anything, that's the thing you need to worry about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T10:06:26-07:00","id":681070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/129553-so-about-red-stick?p=681060#post681060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still a moot point though. If you've gotten the attention of an entire nation's military (not just whatever their Tier 3 hunter org is), you've done goofed and made yourself an enemy of the Powers That Be will remove any trace of existence to maintain the Veil.<br /> <br /> Of anything, that's the thing you need to worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Red Stick isn't the one telling thousands of ordinary mortals there's a werewolf they have to hunt. If the game worked that way, which it doesn't, whoever's in charge would be removed by the 'Powers That Be.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T10:48:46-07:00","id":681145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/129553-so-about-red-stick?p=681070#post681070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Red Stick isn't the one telling thousands of ordinary mortals there's a werewolf they have to hunt. If the game worked that way, which it doesn't, whoever's in charge would be removed by the 'Powers That Be.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the train of thought up until this point was directed at the statement of an entire nation's army plus a werewolf tribe would be needed to put him down (which is incorrect) which assumes that Red Stick (or the Pure tribe that follows) is the aggressing entity. <br /> <br /> If it's the other way around, then things get more interesting and a more interesting story develops.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T11:01:45-07:00","id":681161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/129553-so-about-red-stick?p=681145#post681145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the train of thought up until this point was directed at the statement of an entire nation's army plus a werewolf tribe would be needed to put him down (which is incorrect)</div> </div> </div> </div>Your train of thought is off the rails, considering that was a clearly unserious response-to-a-response from the person who <i>asked </i>how much firepower would be needed after they were reminded that werewolves in the killing form shrug off any damage that isn't rollover or magically enforced and that statement was made <i>over a year ago.</i><br /> <br /> You are wasting everyone's time and engaging in an even more ridiculous pissing contest than the one immediately preceding this one. It's unwelcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></